  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_d42edf310d63401ea06ab3443c351318",
      "statement": "The ACME flow has two entry points: ACMECreateCertFlow (used by step ca certificate) generates a key and writes both the certificate chain and the private key serialized with 0600, or prints the attestation URI instead of a key file for attestation flows; ACMESignCSRFlow (used by step ca sign) submits an existing CSR and writes only the certificate file.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acme_flow.go#L13-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:448b8caa9b3c5ed61b01ea62243fd8c4af66a42b84065f83cd46fa6f4b0eb22d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acme_flow.go#L46-L62",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:771254191f4df820a58fe2fd36fa684954bba28047a4d8dd837a134676835bcf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f4c5d43b567a49f3af42f11520229419",
      "statement": "newACMEFlow enforces flow invariants: --offline is rejected because offline mode and ACME are mutually exclusive; --standalone and --webroot are mutually exclusive and standalone is forced when neither is set; and the ACME directory is taken from --acme or derived as <caURL>/acme/<provisioner>/directory, requiring a provisioner name.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acmeutils.go#L625-L666",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4828dc73965d5e5c880f51fd11dce6e87f07211b3a7f60aaadaef90e3791d4ae:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6ae17d194cb64098a44c7ffe490db009",
      "statement": "ACME SAN validation rejects email and URI SANs outright and rejects wildcard DNS names because dns-01 validation is not implemented in this client; only dns and ip identifiers are supported.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acmeutils.go#L285-L297",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b113ec492b4789c76051ae635111295facb589ff7026397820c0a1ab039f98ae:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b82c51911dc9428387bb5ac83bc3af12",
      "statement": "ACME client trust is resolved by getClientTruststoreOption: with --root (or the default STEPPATH root) present the local root is used via ca.WithRootFile; when --acme targets a non-step CA the local root is merged into the system cert pool; with no local root the system store alone is used.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acmeutils.go#L668-L708",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4a2d35b1b0142caaeef8187f2b357165243326486068d2cd1f584304b94ed713:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6300c1c769974bc5b4a16b6264db5011",
      "statement": "When the ACME directory URL contains letsencrypt, the client rejects --not-before/--not-after (Let's Encrypt does not support NotBefore/NotAfter on orders and issues ~3-month certificates) and appends the subject to the DNS identifiers if missing, since Let's Encrypt requires the Common Name to also be a SAN.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acmeutils.go#L319-L350",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fc2e856a38b4e820af9536a1935f396f2f9f08b1463e43905e98ac8ee0f340f7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8b01440d7cf7469ab21338209b29b230",
      "statement": "Each ACME authorization is validated by exactly one challenge: http-01 normally, or device-attest-01 when --attestation-uri is set; attestation orders carry a single permanent-identifier identifier and do not accept other SANs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acmeutils.go#L196-L232",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b4c2c95e05285e08a399a66aa95b45f6e1b09eecb0f5951639912957863f6753:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acmeutils.go#L718-L740",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:be663367509c3c4662f68e05fee07a0724fba0f7c93187f65987b5adb0dbec7c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4ea30e28ecda4447ba6866e7645f9ada",
      "statement": "In standalone mode the client starts a local HTTP server on --http-listen (default :80) serving /.well-known/acme-challenge/<token> with the ACME key authorization, and shuts it down with a 1-second grace period after validation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acmeutils.go#L47-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:203c2fdf65b3fd26016bc4270b9a1e5efee7f572a4bcb03707ceff0f91180bde:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acmeutils.go#L94-L108",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1416f89f1d398f91ef56c3fca0dab9418f042d34d4667bbff5121a3d7bb89900:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2caf1e3e7ffd450ba7bb914768467ba9",
      "statement": "In webroot mode the key authorization is written to <webroot>/.well-known/acme-challenge/<token> with directories created 0755 and files 0644 by design, because the web server serving the challenge typically runs as a different user than the step process; cleanup removes the challenge file.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acmeutils.go#L124-L157",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1950301b7251f0ecd23a721ba696a676df796a48670b220e4c4c5a30a891f9d6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_adff9c2d08fa4bed880ef68fbb1d6d13",
      "statement": "After serving the challenge, the client triggers CA validation and polls getChallengeStatus up to 10 times (5s apart for http-01, 2s for device attestation) until the challenge is valid, breaking early on invalid, then runs mode cleanup; failure surfaces the challenge's ACME error detail including subproblems.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acmeutils.go#L159-L194",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1437d4acf49f9c618f92921965ff21a51e810742b487eef144f754ab7a999af5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acmeutils.go#L514-L549",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:317beb2fa989c1531a5b2ce76915600dcf96e562bfcde2c130a6ed8ecaa2ac5e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_eba6ac8597264a55a8a974828fabe118",
      "statement": "finalizeOrder polls the order until status ready (up to ~10 one-second iterations), posts the CSR to the finalize URL, then polls until status valid, erroring with the order contents if either deadline passes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acmeutils.go#L234-L283",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:76325ec18d7936266aebba4f1cb7a51606fff1e585c2e4e18351840a1c0bb550:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_809d5c86320244f58222f1da54c044aa",
      "statement": "The issued leaf plus chain are fetched from the certificate URL and written as a full-chain PEM with 0600 via fileutil.WriteFile; for TPM-backed attestation flows the chain is additionally stored on the TPM key via the go.step.sm/crypto tpm package using --tpm-storage-directory.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acmeutils.go#L833-L862",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ad9cc1784a7fcd745933995ee20244c86de564987c01c3d4a7748c80a8de2dfc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acmeutils.go#L867-L880",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:14ab2d26b988f0ad557cef9b1dd56ea65782981ca4e86367d4bcf0733549ff41:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f3efdecbf1eb426e9d22a0e4c73e4449",
      "statement": "Device-attest-01 proves possession of a hardware-backed key: a tpmkms: attestation URI routes to the TPM flow, otherwise cryptoutil.CreateAttestor builds an attestor; the key authorization is signed (ES256 for P-256 ECDSA, RS256 for RSA, EdDSA for Ed25519), CBOR-encoded, and posted in a step-format attestation object with x5c certificate chain, and validation is synchronous server-side.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/acmeutils.go#L403-L512",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6169fb419637da40bb255537945aa1e4d03314632021bf5d276c8ef0baa31994:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/tpm.go#L40-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:92419e63f50e335f063ce460ebff09b83e88d8d82e59f7de555121d10dbe045a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_baca41ee8b4349cc98a326c3e7f5914c",
      "statement": "step ca acme manages External Account Binding keys through the CA Admin API (CreateExternalAccountKey, pagination, removal), printing key ID, provisioner, base64url-encoded HMAC key and reference; when the CA reports the operation as not implemented the error is rewritten to point at Smallstep Certificate Manager.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/acme/acme.go#L10-L20",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:63290cc69882dd1df17b953e8175985de966df95ed7863069ee2ab24fd6571ad:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/acme/eab/add.go#L60-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5613e0779d5af4415bd031ca0fb7595f848a3567d2b592169489258aa0505db0:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/acme/eab/eab.go#L81-L89",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e2e4a599bad99bfc311261bcc8d71694420063f09caf403ce78f1148e41395be:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_37cf2983b6db4b98b434487ce733b9f7",
      "statement": "eab list pages through keys with cursor pagination (defaulting to 100 per page, overridable with --limit), masks key material as *****, and optionally pipes output to $PAGER — rejecting PAGER values containing shell metacharacters and validating it exists on PATH.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/acme/eab/list.go#L84-L177",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a77d4aeba210277fef5ddce8f0725741be0c3463c85b423aec583a935246fa63:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_76aaa67e5c4c44879a8a1a6a023a97f7",
      "statement": "The pager lifecycle in eab list is guarded by a SIGCHLD handler (non-Windows builds) that stops signal handling and exits the parent process with status 0 when the child (pager) is killed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/acme/eab/sigchild.go#L7-L17",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dc279582a4cd2f089006925959927c12207f7ac127c6a13aed0197aa582dd4b4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_46f99ca8834045858ed5220680fecb16",
      "statement": "The acme management group is additionally exposed as an in-development API via step beta ca acme: the beta command nests ca.BetaCommand(), which itself returns a ca command containing acme.Command().",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/beta/beta.go#L12-L25",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b7d3bc363bb1acffe2e4290c3a718ed5448451551895c22891964be35b24a553:"
