        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bd9d79e710514912b2529ef03594963a",
      "statement": "ACME and SCEP provisioners reject the JWT token flow by design — NewTokenFlow returns ACMETokenError / SCEPTokenError ('do not support token auth flows') because ACME authorization is challenge-based rather than token-based — and step ca certificate exploits the typed ACMETokenError to transparently switch to ACMECreateCertFlow with the provisioner's name; an explicit --acme flag short-circuits to ACME before the token flow is attempted.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/certificate.go#L243-L266",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:536cf739dd89d78015c5e4120966b99c9f291b093beb96646d9c1a6dbd66a545:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/token_flow.go#L176-L179",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8b08f29870cf2a988ce7004d51815db2932d6ce96f99525bfd3e7d61a6aa6427:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/token_flow.go#L78-L98",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:78b3d27ed11a508cbcd5884a0a4ddd93f064226b356cad8094970a481e807872:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8c6c6c72730a4842ac0b87b8e76ebb27",
      "statement": "The ACME client flow has no dedicated unit or integration tests in this repository; utils/cautils tests cover token and offline flows and the integration testscripts do not exercise ACME against a live CA, so behavior is established by the implementation and command documentation.",
